# sync

## BOT

- [ ] **Synchronize calendar** — pull events from Google Calendar and create/update calendardeck cards for the full sync range defined in `sync/SYNC.md`.

- [ ] Read `.flowdeck/.calendardeck/sync/SYNC.md` — extract `Calendar ID`, `Sync Range`, and `Last Sync`. If the file does not exist, stop and note under `## HUMAN` to run `calendardeck-init` first.

- [ ] Validate config before proceeding:
  - If `Calendar ID` is empty or still a placeholder (e.g. `{{CALENDAR_ID}}`, `your-calendar-id@gmail.com`): stop and surface under `## HUMAN` that the Calendar ID must be set in `sync/SYNC.md` before syncing.
  - If `.flowdeck/.flowdeck/_energy-cards/DAY.md.template` does not exist: stop and surface under `## HUMAN` to run `calendardeck-init` first to deploy energy-card templates.

- [ ] Determine the sync date range:
  - If `## HUMAN` below specifies an explicit range (e.g. `range: 2026-06-01–2026-06-30`), use that.
  - Otherwise use the `Sync Range` field from `SYNC.md` (default: current month).
  - Resolve to concrete start/end ISO dates.

- [ ] Fetch events from Google Calendar:
  - Try the claude.ai built-in Google Calendar MCP first:
    - If `mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__authenticate` is available, call it to start OAuth. Then call `mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__list_events` with `calendarId`, `timeMin`, `timeMax`, `singleEvents: true`, `orderBy: startTime`.
  - If the built-in is unavailable, fall back to `@cocal/google-calendar-mcp`:
    - Call `mcp__google_calendar__list_events` with the same parameters.
  - If neither tool is available: call `mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__authenticate` — if that fails too, stop and note under `## HUMAN` to connect Google Calendar in Claude Code settings (Settings → Integrations), then replay this card.

- [ ] For each calendar day in the sync range — whether or not it has events:
  - Compute slug: `YYYYMMDD`.
  - Create `.flowdeck/.calendardeck/{{SLUG}}/` if missing.
  - Write `EVENTS.md` from `.flowdeck/_energy-cards/DAY.md.template` — substitute `{{SLUG}}`, `{{WEEKDAY}}`, `{{DATE_LONG}}`, and `{{EVENTS_TABLE}}` (one row per event: time, title, location, attendees). If the day has zero events, substitute `{{EVENTS_TABLE}}` with `_No events._` so the card is still well-formed.
  - Scaffold `TODO.md` only if it does not exist — do not overwrite. Use this template:

    ```
    # {{SLUG}}

    {{WEEKDAY}}, {{DATE_LONG}}

    ## BOT

    ## HUMAN

    ## ACTIONS

    <!-- Move an item to ## BOT to activate it, then play this card. -->

    - [ ] send-to-gcal — [Title | YYYY-MM-DD | HH:MM–HH:MM | optional description]
    - [ ] sync-day — re-fetch events for this day only
    ```

- [ ] For each week spanned by the sync range:
  - Compute slug: `{{YYYYMM}}W{{N}}` where N = `ceil(first_day_of_week_in_month / 7)`.
  - Create `.flowdeck/.calendardeck/{{SLUG}}/` if missing.
  - Write `SUMMARY.md` from `.flowdeck/_energy-cards/WEEK.md.template`.
  - Scaffold `TODO.md` only if it does not exist:

    ```
    # {{SLUG}}

    Week {{N}} of {{MONTH_LONG}} — {{DATE_RANGE}}

    ## BOT

    ## HUMAN

    ## ACTIONS

    - [ ] send-to-gcal — [Title | YYYY-MM-DD | HH:MM–HH:MM | optional description]
    ```

- [ ] For each month spanned by the sync range:
  - Compute slug: `{{YYYYMM}}`.
  - Write `SUMMARY.md` from `.flowdeck/_energy-cards/MONTH.md.template`.
  - Scaffold `TODO.md` only if it does not exist:

    ```
    # {{YYYYMM}}

    {{MONTH_LONG}} {{YYYY}}

    ## BOT

    ## HUMAN

    ## ACTIONS

    - [ ] send-to-gcal — [Title | YYYY-MM-DD | HH:MM–HH:MM | optional description]
    ```

- [ ] For each year spanned by the sync range:
  - Compute slug: `{{YYYY}}`.
  - Write `SUMMARY.md` from `.flowdeck/_energy-cards/YEAR.md.template`.
  - Scaffold `TODO.md` only if it does not exist:

    ```
    # {{YYYY}}

    ## BOT

    ## HUMAN

    ## ACTIONS

    - [ ] send-to-gcal — [Title | YYYY-MM-DD | HH:MM–HH:MM | optional description]
    ```

- [ ] Append a row to the `## Run Log` table in `sync/SYNC.md`:
  | {{TODAY}} | {{RANGE}} | {{DAYS_SYNCED}} | {{EVENTS_FETCHED}} | {{CARDS_CREATED}} | {{CARDS_UPDATED}} |

- [ ] Surface a sync summary under `## HUMAN`: range synced, number of events fetched, cards created, cards updated.

